WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.480
Speaker 1: Donald Trump has received disastrous&nbsp;
news from his own former lawyer, Ty Cobb.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:17.640
His name is really Ty Cobb. Ty Cobb believes&nbsp;
Trump will end up convicted and in prison&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:26.160
for one of Trump's own former lawyers to say&nbsp;
this is really something. Donald Trump's former&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:32.940
attorney has boldly predicted that the former&nbsp;
president is going to jail as the criminal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:37.320
investigation into the trove of classified&nbsp;
documents found at Mar a Lago continues to heat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:43.260
up. Ty Cobb, who worked as a White House attorney&nbsp;
for the Trump administration from July 2017 to May&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:50.760
2018, said to CNN The evidence against Trump will&nbsp;
lead to a conviction and prison time. Reminder,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:56.624
this is separate from Georgia, where an indictment&nbsp;
may be coming. This is separate from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.624 --> 00:01:01.980
preexisting arrest and indictment of Trump. This&nbsp;
is its own. This is for the documents in Florida.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:09.720
Quote, I wouldn't necessarily expand the case&nbsp;
to try to prove the Espionage Act piece of it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:13.920
because there's so much evidence of guilty&nbsp;
knowledge on the espionage piece that all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:19.920
they really have to do is show that Trump move&nbsp;
these documents at various times when DOJ was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:26.040
either demanding them or actually present that he&nbsp;
filed falsely with the Justice Department, had his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:31.020
lawyers file falsely with the Justice Department&nbsp;
and affidavit to the effect that none existed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:35.280
meaning no documents, which was shattered&nbsp;
by the documents they discovered after the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:43.200
search and the many other misrepresentations.&nbsp;
Yes, I do think he will go to jail on it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:50.340
Business Insider reports a former White House&nbsp;
lawyer believes Trump will go to jail. Ty Cobb&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:55.320
said there was so much evidence of guilty&nbsp;
knowledge. As investigations continue, the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.320 --> 00:02:01.860
DOJ is probing whether Trump obstructed justice&nbsp;
in bringing classified documents to Mar a Lago.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:07.920
If other people did what Trump did, they&nbsp;
would certainly be prosecuted. Now, you know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:12.840
sometimes you'll see legal analysts or not.&nbsp;
Usually it's more like non-legal Analysts say&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:17.880
anybody who did this would be convicted&nbsp;
and sentenced to prison. Conviction is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:22.680
a much different thing. Right. The criminal&nbsp;
standard of guilt beyond a reasonable doubt,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:28.980
It's very hard to predict conviction. But what we&nbsp;
can say with certainty is that if other people did&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:33.480
what Trump did with regard to the documents, they&nbsp;
would certainly be prosecuted. And then we would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:37.740
look at whether they get convicted. And the most&nbsp;
important aspect of all of this is that no one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:45.300
should be above the law, should being the critical&nbsp;
word. The last part of this speculating on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:51.780
outcome of ongoing investigations in a sense can&nbsp;
be misleading. And it is true that when you hear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:56.580
a lawyer like Ty Cobb say, you go, Wow, this this&nbsp;
is not just a random lawyer. This is not a random&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.580 --> 00:03:02.880
left wing lawyer. This is a lawyer who worked&nbsp;
for Trump. And that does carry strength. And so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:08.520
I think we should listen to what Ty Cobb says.&nbsp;
At the same time, investigations can be fickle.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:14.280
These things have to run their course. We want&nbsp;
impartiality when it comes to the justice system.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:19.620
And so when Ty Cobb makes these predictions,&nbsp;
they're worth noting, given his knowledge and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:25.020
associations with four former President Donald&nbsp;
Trump. But also, we should approach all of it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:31.920
with caution. Let the investigations play out and&nbsp;
be guided by evidence. And for the time being, I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:38.100
have every reason to believe that that is exactly&nbsp;
what the Justice Department has been doing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:45.960
I can't imagine if you are Trump, you're thrilled&nbsp;
when your own former lawyer says, I think you're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:51.540
going to prison. But let's wait and see, because&nbsp;
it's certainly one of many possible outcomes here

